  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on which lottery assigns more probability to unfavorable outcomes (i.e., higher probability of any loss), favoring the more right-skewed one (A). The individual, however, focuses on the severity of the loss in B, not the probability of loss. The individual’s reasoning is consistent with loss aversion or sensitivity to worst-case outcomes, not with assessing skewness. While both the reason and the individual choose A, the justification differs: the reason prefers A due to higher probability of loss (more right-skew), while the individual avoids B due to the size of the loss. There is no evidence the individual considered the relative probabilities of loss as indicative of skewness. The information considered (loss magnitude) and the justification (unacceptability of large loss) do not align with the skewness-based rule. Therefore, it is unlikely the individual used the skewness reason.",
