lity is assigned to unfavorable as opposed to favorable outcomes' — this contradicts standard statistical skewness. According to this definition, a lottery with higher probability of unfavorable outcomes is more right-skewed. In this case, 'unfavorable' = any loss, 'favorable' = 0€. So Lottery A has 25% unfavorable, 75% favorable. Lottery B has 50% unfavorable, 50% favorable. So B has a greater portion of probability on unfavorable outcomes and thus, by this non-standard definition, is more right-skewed. Therefore, the reason would prefer Lottery B. The reason can be applied: relevant information is the probability of unfavorable (loss) outcomes. Lottery B has higher probability of loss (50%) vs A (25%), so B is more right-skewed under this definition, and thus preferred.",
